f the guitar and its heavily-accented vocals describing life's hardships. A common joke runs that if one plays a country song backwards, the singer's child recovers from an illness.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Miley Cyrus", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Post Malone", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "dance-pop": {"genre": "dance-pop", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Dance-pop is a style of electronic dance music and a subgenre of pop music that evolved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 184215, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": 59603, "best_position": 63}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 52291, "best_position": 88}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Addison Rae", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charlie Puth", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "PUN", "streams": 609628, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Cigarettes After Sex", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ellie Goulding", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 184215, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 52291, "best_position": 88}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Addison Rae", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chase Atlantic", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "YOUNGOHM", "streams": 275055, "best_position": 36}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Joji", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kanye West", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 184215, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Hearts2Hearts", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jennie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Velvet", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "TWICE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "neo soul": {"genre": "neo soul", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Neo soul (also written neo-soul) is a subgenre of soul, usually blending a hybrid of 1970s-influenced soul music with influences from jazz, funk, hip-hop & electronica. It may also include influences from African, Asian, Latin, rock-n-roll and house music, depending on the artist.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charlie Puth", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daniel Caesar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kali Uchis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Olivia Dean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ravyn Lenae", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "SZA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "th", "country_name": "Thailand", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 184215, "